.TH MINIOS-KERNEL 1 "August 2026" "MiniOS Kernel Manager 1.2.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
minios-kernel \- Command-line tool for managing MiniOS kernels
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minios-kernel
.RI [ --help ]
.br
.B minios-kernel
.RB [ --json ]
.B list
.br
.B minios-kernel
.RB [ --json ]
.B activate
.I kernel-version
.br
.B minios-kernel
.RB [ --json ]
.B info
.RI [ kernel-version ]
.br
.B minios-kernel
.RB [ --json ]
.B package
.RB { --repo
.I package
.RB | --deb
.IR file... }
.B -o
.I output-dir
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B minios-kernel
.RB [ --json ]
.B status
.br
.B minios-kernel
.RB [ --json ]
.B delete
.I kernel-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minios-kernel
is a command-line utility for managing Linux kernels in the MiniOS distribution. Requires root privileges.
.PP
This tool serves as both a standalone CLI utility and the backend for the graphical
.BR minios-kernel-manager .
It handles kernel packaging, activation, and provides detailed kernel information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show the built-in help message and exit.
.TP
.B --json
Output results in JSON format. Can be used with any command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List available kernels with their status.
.TP
.BI activate " kernel-version"
Activate the specified kernel version for the next boot.
.TP
.BI info " [kernel-version]"
Show information about a kernel. If no version specified, shows current active kernel.
.TP
.B package
Package a kernel from a repository or one or more local .deb files.
.TP
.B status
Check MiniOS directory status and write permissions.
.TP
.BI delete " kernel-version"
Delete the specified packaged kernel from the repository.
.SH PACKAGE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --repo " package-name"
Download and package a real versioned kernel package from the existing system
APT configuration. Tracking metapackages such as linux-image-amd64 are rejected.
.TP
.BI --deb " deb-file..."
Package a kernel from one or more local .deb files. Debian split kernels require
a coherent image, binary, base, and modules set; Ubuntu split kernels require
the matching image and modules packages, plus modules-extra when selected.
.TP
.BI "-o, --output " output-dir
Directory to save packaged kernel files. Required.
.TP
.BI --sqfs-comp " method"
Compression method for SquashFS image. Default: \fBzstd\fR.
.TP
.BI --temp-dir " directory"
Custom temporary directory (must have at least 1024MB free space).
.TP
.B --force-update
Run apt update before repository packaging. Without this option, the existing
system package lists are used without an age gate.
.SH PACKAGING
Repository mode resolves matching linux-modules packages automatically. Local
mode accepts multiple packages for split kernels. The output includes the
kernel image, initramfs, and SquashFS module; selected dpkg metadata is retained
inside the SquashFS at
.IR /usr/share/minios/kernel-dpkg/ .
.PP
Repository downloads are temporary workspace inputs and are removed after
success or handled failure. Local input archives remain caller-owned. New
bundles use canonical frozen format 1 with a manual held image package, automatic
subordinate kernel packages, and no embedded repository configuration.
.PP
The canonical runtime module path is /lib/modules/<version>. The physical path
stored in the bundle follows the running base system: lib/modules on traditional
layouts or usr/lib/modules when /lib is usrmerged. Packaging refuses an existing
same-version module tree rather than mix it with a different package revision.
.PP
When a writable MiniOS root is detected and the output is not already the
repository directory, the completed package is staged atomically into
.IR <MiniOS-root>/kernels/<version> .
.PP
Packaging requires a MiniOS live runtime with mkdracut or mkinitrfs under
.IR /run/initramfs ,
plus mksquashfs, depmod, and dpkg-deb. Repository mode also requires APT.
.SH ENCRYPTED PERSISTENCE
When the running initrd advertises encrypted persistence, the replacement
kernel must provide dm-crypt support. The generated initramfs is checked for
cryptsetup, dm-crypt.ko, and etc/minios-initramfs-crypt. Packaging fails when
those safeguards cannot be preserved.
.SH ACTIVATION
Activation requires a complete repository entry containing the SquashFS,
kernel image, and initramfs. Boot files and bootloader configuration are updated
atomically and restored if activation fails. GRUB configuration is required;
SYSLINUX configuration is updated when present. Activation affects the next
boot and does not reboot the machine.
.PP
Activation accepts Manager-produced frozen format-1 bundles and canonical
tracked bundles produced by 01-kernel. The legacy 1.2.1 metadata shape is
accepted only by the live activation compatibility path.
.SH EXAMPLES
List available kernels:
.RS
.B sudo minios-kernel list
.RE
.PP
Activate a specific kernel:
.RS
.B sudo minios-kernel activate 6.12.38+deb13-amd64
.RE
.PP
Package kernel from repository:
.RS
.B sudo minios-kernel package --repo linux-image-6.12.38+deb13-amd64 -o /tmp/output
.RE
.PP
Package kernel from local .deb file:
.RS
.B sudo minios-kernel package --deb kernel.deb -o /tmp/output
.RE
.PP
Delete a packaged kernel:
.RS
.B sudo minios-kernel delete 6.12.38+deb13-amd64
.RE
.SH JSON OUTPUT
When using the \fB--json\fR option, commands return structured data:
.TP
.B list
Returns array of kernels with version, status, and metadata.
.TP
.B activate
Returns success status and activation details.
.TP
.B info
Returns kernel information including version, status, and system paths.
.TP
.B package
Returns progress updates during packaging and final success status.
.TP
.B status
Returns MiniOS directory status and filesystem information.
.TP
.B delete
Returns success status and deletion details.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/initramfs/memory/data/minios/
Preferred MiniOS root in the standard runtime.
.TP
.I /lib/live/mount/medium/minios/
Fallback MiniOS root on a mounted live medium.
.TP
.I <MiniOS-root>/kernels/<version>/
Repository for inactive packaged kernels.
.TP
.I <MiniOS-root>/boot/vmlinuz-*
Active kernel image.
.TP
.I <MiniOS-root>/boot/initrfs-*.img
Active initramfs image.
.TP
.I <MiniOS-root>/01-kernel-*.sb
Active SquashFS kernel modules.
.TP
.I <MiniOS-root>/boot/active-kernel
Active version marker.
